How far can a squeeze by SanDisk go? Qiuqiu lays out a trading script above 1600

@Genius Girl Qiuqiu This live stream revolves around one core question: After SanDisk quickly surges, should you follow the trend or wait for the price to rise further before shorting? Her answer is very clear—on the short term, the bias remains bullish, but you must separate “direction judgment” from “position management.” She repeatedly stressed: don’t mechanically guess the top just because prices have been rising consecutively, and don’t use the long-vs-short ratio or liquidation-map logic commonly seen in the crypto圈 to explain the pre-market and opening-session moves in U.S. stocks.

Strength is not a reason to short; 1600 is the key observation level
